  gallery={gallery}
  prev={{ href: '/hunziker-areal/', label: 'Hunziker Areal' }}
  next={{ href: '/la-balma/', label: 'La Balma' }}
>
  <section class="case-reading mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-6 pt-12 sm:px-12">
    <p>Gleis 21, completed in Vienna in 2019, includes 34 homes and four commercial spaces in a timber-hybrid building. The architect’s account names the resident group, facilitator realitylab and nonprofit developer Schwarzatal: collective housing still involves a professional delivery team. <a class="source-link" href="https://www.einszueins.at/project/baugruppe-hauptbahnhof-gleis-21/">[Project source]</a></p>
    <p>Cultural and media activities at ground level address the wider neighborhood. Shared roof facilities serve residents; the sauna and library should not be described as public ground-floor attractions. The project emerged through a concept-based site process in Sonnwendviertel.</p>
    <h2>Public downstairs. Shared upstairs. Private at home.</h2>
    <p>Those three levels of access make a useful conversation starter. A building can contribute to the street without asking residents to surrender all privacy. Clear thresholds, booking rules and separate access can help the different activities coexist.</p>
    <p>A concept-based land competition is worth studying, but its rules cannot simply be transplanted overnight. Local land-disposition law, funding, selection fairness and delivery capacity need their own process. Good intentions should be part of a proposal that can actually be delivered.</p>
    <aside class="research-note mt-8">Reading lens: project publications document the place and its intended design. They are not independent evaluations of affordability, energy performance or how every resident experiences life there. The questions here are our interpretation.</aside>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="lessons">
<li>Pair resident ambition with experienced facilitation, development and operations.</li>
<li>Differentiate public cultural space from resident amenities in both plans and descriptions.</li>
<li>Evaluate land proposals on transparent criteria, including affordability and realistic delivery, with local legal review.</li>
</Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="sources"><a href="https://gleis21.wien/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/Infopaket_Juni-2023-1.pdf">Gleis 21 resident information (PDF)</a> · <a href="https://www.einszueins.at/project/baugruppe-hauptbahnhof-gleis-21/">einszueins · Gleis 21 project account</a>. Reviewed October 2026. Approximate counts are identified; population changes over time.</Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
